hiring great people is core to every  business but finding the right talent is  often the tricky part traditional job  sites aim to help people find jobs and  jobs find people but can have difficulty  returning relevant results let's dive  into how you can use Google's cloud  talent solution to leverage machine  learning and create a better job search  experience see large companies may have  their own internal hiring and recruiting  teams whereas smaller companies might  use off-the-shelf talent solutions but  both want quality results for candidates  and job postings trying to match these  together may sound simple on the surface  but traditional keyword searching is too  simplistic and gets choked up in some  situations such as hidden or extraneous  keywords also known as keyword stuffing  job postings that require five years of  experience in a technology that's really  only been around for two years and  things like typos acronyms and overuse  of technical jargon what exactly is a  wreck and asset prot one ultimately  these lead to poor experiences and bad  candidate fits so Google used machine  learning also called ml to create a  customizable job searching experience  the cloud talent solution job search API  is designed to power the job search  experience with built-in machine  learning algorithms in short you send  your job listing information over such  as the company and job details to the  job search API the API analyzes the job  data to develop an understanding of the  jobs once jobs have been indexed by the  API you can search against the jobs and  get search results by relevance or other  sorting preferences which we'll talk  about in future videos there are four  common use cases that typically leverage  a solution like this job boards where  the site returns a list of jobs to job  seekers career site providers that  provide career site services to client  companies staffing agencies which  provide short or long term employees to  clients and applicant tracking systems  which are used by companies to track  applicants through the hiring process  the job search API is designed to be  modified to best fit with your needs and  the api's performance can vary  significantly based on how its  configured also it's worth noting that  the job search API is not to be confused  with the jobs indexing API that  facilitates jobs showing up on  google.com search  there's a separate indexing API to have  job listings show up on searches that  people make on google.com there's a link  for this in the description if you want  to learn more about that but the cloud  talent solution job search API does much  more when it's integrated into your job  search solution with all that being said  let's talk about how to actually  implement the job search API in our next  video we'll go over the API in greater  detail planning steps and talk more  about implementation strategies thanks  for watching and remember when looking  for talent it's ok to keep your head in  the cloud
 

